        "itemId": 17592186649259,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
        "mathAcademyId": null,
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "The minimum set is $a_{42}$ and $a_{43}$. Replace these 2 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 3, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{42}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 2, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. Restoring $a_{43}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 3, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. No set with fewer than 2 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero.",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186627931",
        "title": "Practice"
      },
      "total": 9
    },
