        "itemId": 17592186649953,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
        "mathAcademyId": null,
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "- $F$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 2 rows and 3 columns.\n\n- $H$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 2 rows and 3 columns.\n\n- $M$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\nTherefore, only $M$ is a diagonal matrix.",
