        "itemId": 17592186649955,
        "kind": "question",
        "knowledgePoint": null,
        "markdown": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $U$ into the matrix $V$, where\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nV=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
        "mathAcademyId": "q-72850",
        "requiresCalculator": null,
        "solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $1$st row and the $3$rd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $1$st and the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & \\,{R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$",
        "status": "correct",
        "stepId": "17592186627936",
        "title": "Practice"
      },
      "total": 9
